# Story 4.3 — env for serving dispatch-send LOCALLY against the provider mock (tests/provider-mock.ts).
# No secrets here: the mock accepts any key, and this cron secret only guards the locally served function.
#   supabase functions serve dispatch-send --env-file supabase/mock.env --no-verify-jwt
# The Edge Runtime container reaches the mock on the host through host.docker.internal (Linux CI: --add-host).
# The real provider's PROVIDER_BASE_URL / PROVIDER_API_KEY and the real CRON_SECRET live in the git-ignored
# supabase/.env and in the hosted function secrets (`supabase secrets set`) — never in this file.
PROVIDER_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8787
PROVIDER_API_KEY=mock
CRON_SECRET=local-cron-secret
# DISPATCH_RETRY_ENABLED is deliberately NOT set here (Story 6.2): unset ⇒ a provider 5xx / timeout marks the send
# `partial` immediately (D-7). Story 6.3 adds `DISPATCH_RETRY_ENABLED=on` here and in the hosted secrets in the same
# step that enables the dispatch-sweep cron job.
